[2026-09-10T01:44:55Z] iter-9: DRIVER pose authored. Solved roll about the shaft = 147.55 deg, residual azimuth 0.0000 deg. NOT the 174.34 deg plan-azimuth error - the shaft carries the lie angle, so a roll of theta does not move the plan azimuth by theta; reading the error off as the roll would have left ~27 deg of open face. ClubSlot.localRotation (0.310162,0.173976,0.232012,0.905374) -> (-0.136109,0.917925,0.362636,0.085924). localPosition and ClubStart/ClubEnd untouched (both lie ON the roll axis, so club.headAtBall 0.0085 cannot move). Head-mesh centre to ball in plan 0.0464 -> 0.0316 m. ALSO FIXED a pre-existing harness brace bug: sections 3+4 (stance.followsHeading, club.bothPresent/driverDefault/putterSwap/driverSwapBack and the whole PuttGripOnGreen putt-address measurement) were nested inside "if (slot != null && hasQuaterniusFingers)" and so had never run on a Mixamo run - not even as SKIP. Confirmed pre-existing: the committed iter-8 golfer_invariants_mixamo.json lacks all five ids. Braces balanced by accident, so it compiled.

[2026-09-10T01:48:04Z] iter-9: PUTTER pose authored. Solved roll at the putt address = -121.35 deg, residual 0.0000. PutterSlot.localRotation (0.310162,0.173976,0.232012,0.905374) -> (0.354187,-0.704149,-0.156786,0.595101); localPosition untouched. Driver re-verified after authoring: club.faceSquare PASS, leading edge vs aim 89.9957 deg, azimuth error 0.0000 deg, solved residual roll 0.0000 deg. Brace fix restored 6 rows, all PASS (stance.followsHeading, club.bothPresent, club.driverDefault, club.putterSwap, club.driverSwapBack); pass 25 -> 31. Added a pose-provenance log (animator state/normTime/inTransition, GripTarget + both hand world rotations, golfer-to-ball) because the putt solve reported a GripTarget rotation bit-identical to the drive address AND a head-to-ball of 152.77 m - PuttGripOnGreen moves the BALL to the green without re-placing the GOLFER. Next: rig-off baseline run, then THE acceptance run.

[2026-09-10T01:56:42Z] iter-9: CESAR NOTE mid-run - "The club is a bit too high for the hand pose. It should be a bit lower so it looks inside the cupped hands and not above them." Measured instead of nudged: fist centre = centroid of the 8 non-thumb MCP+PIP joints per hand (8/8 bones found both hands), seat = midpoint. Shaft missed the fists hollow by 0.0969 m; seat station y=0.1032 was already ON the grip (spans -0.110..+0.157), so it was a pure sideways miss. TRANSLATE would have cost club.headAtBall 0.0085 -> 0.0922 m (over the 0.05 gate), so PIVOT about the head instead: head stays exactly on the ball, lie changes 7.03 deg (driver) / 10.80 deg total (putter), then the roll re-solved about the new shaft. Driver derived twice independently (world-space and GripTarget-space) agreeing to 1e-5. FINAL: ClubSlot pos (0.04038,0.05156,-0.06853) rot (-0.156203,0.891029,0.414258,0.100295); PutterSlot pos (0.04229,0.05664,-0.07076) rot (0.438293,-0.661561,-0.167756,0.584889). Residual seat miss 0.00000 m BOTH slots. Pose provenance settled: at the putt sample animator=Address_Putt normTime 0 notInTransition, yet GripTarget and BOTH hand world rotations are bit-identical to Address_Drive - the two address clips share their hand keys, so the putter roll is valid. Also found: PuttGripOnGreen moves the BALL to the green without re-placing the GOLFER (golfer-to-ball 152.70 m), so distances in that section are meaningless; the roll solve is direction-only and heading-invariant, so unaffected.

[2026-09-10T02:04:38Z] iter-9: CESAR NOTE 2 - "A bit too low now, it goes through the left hand.s pinky. But close. The club should not go through any fingers/hand." Measured all 32 finger/hand joints beside the grip as radii from the shaft axis. FINDING: the clip.s two fists do NOT share a tunnel - seating the shaft on the midpoint of the two fist centres put it in the gap BETWEEN them (each centre ~23mm off-axis on OPPOSITE sides), so it clipped R.Ring3 (0.0041 m), R.Mid2 (0.0064), L.Ring2/L.Mid2 (0.0129) - all inside the grip surface at 0.0136 m. Clearance grows MONOTONICALLY with distance past ~25mm, i.e. the max-min optimum is simply to leave the hands: there is NO axis that is inside the fists and touching nothing. Solved instead for the CLOSEST axis at which no finger bone is within grip surface 0.0136 + fingerRadius 0.00683 = 0.0204 m: offset 0.0311 m at slot-local (x+0.01115, z+0.02903), worst clearance 0.0205 m, pinned symmetrically between R.Ring2 and L.Pinky2 (both 0.0205). Still 3x closer to the hands than the original 0.0969 m miss. Applied as a pivot about the on-axis head point (driver 2.251 deg, putter 3.336 deg) so club.headAtBall is preserved, roll re-solved after each. FINAL: ClubSlot pos (0.03009,0.07460,-0.09264) rot (-0.144565,0.882671,0.433683,0.109142); PutterSlot pos (0.03073,0.08187,-0.09457) rot (0.450949,-0.651749,-0.192278,0.578703).

[2026-09-10T02:40:05Z] iter-9b: Cesar rejected all three placements ("below both hands" on the 31mm one) and chose AUTHOR A HAND POSE, adding "you can also bend the wrists slightly if needed". Root cause measured: fists 46.4mm apart PERPENDICULAR to the shaft vs 37.7mm along it - side by side across the club, not threaded on it. Also: "stop restoring profile in this machine. We will keep testing the golfer." -> switched back to iOS-Full-Golfer, memory project_pc_golfer_build_profile.md rewritten. Key geometric insight for the pose: at the fist-centroid seat the fingertips are 4-20mm from the axis while contact is 20.4mm, i.e. the clip fists are TIGHTER than the grip, so the pose OPENS them slightly - a small change, and the opposite of the bisect-to-cap wrap that made claws. New pose path only; ApplyGripPose/WrapJoint untouched.

[2026-09-10T02:52:30Z] iter-9b: held-grip pose landing. Run 1 (fist-centre seat, tip objective): miss 0.0072, worst clearance 0.0036. Run 2 (GripSeatInHand = knuckle row + contact along the palm normal; curl objective = closest MOVABLE joint, j[0] excluded because a joint rotation does not move itself): miss 0.0026, worst 0.0062. Run 3 identical to run 2 - the C# default change was shadowed by the SERIALIZED prefab value (heldOpenMaxDeg stayed 30); real lesson, set it on the prefab. Run 4 (knuckle-row twist about the arm axis through the seat + heldOpenMaxDeg 45): miss 0.0032, worst 0.0073. VISUAL: the club now runs THROUGH BOTH HANDS with the trail hand curling round the grip - the thing Cesar asked for. Remaining: lead fingers still splay and some overlap the grip (worst 0.0073 vs grip surface 0.0136). shaftRadius corrected 0.008727 -> 0.013575, measured off the Grip mesh bounds (0.02715 across) - the old value would have seated every fingertip ~5mm inside the mesh.

